  "observations": [
    "Baseline real-seat probes in both engines show native state 1 but DOM checked false for an initially checked mixed checkbox; labels bypass native action. Raw observations are separate from formal qualification.",
    "Final Chromium form suite passes 101 rows/28 complete images; Firefox 102/28 adds browser-owned-UI preservation. Real pointer, key and label paths cover four checked/mixed combinations, original trusted events, checked/mixed rollback on cancellation and whole native pixels. Application overrides, disabled/cancelled/interactive/implicit labels, untrusted programmatic/nested activation, button/input-button/submit/reset and cancellation retain original engine semantics.",
    "Final radio group/pointer/label and button/text regressions use the same held final fixtures; Firefox popup geometry/model/sizing also checks the changed shared capture harness. The dedicated checkbox/radio run additionally checks renderer/helper loss and original sandbox flags. The dedicated legacy-input mode intentionally disables optional matrix groups/buttons; matrix mode is qualified separately by the broad radio suites. Its 40 rows/15 complete images pass, including six-control renderer cleanup, retained original mouse/key input after helper loss and Seccomp=2/NoNewPrivs=1. Combined scoped total is 732 rows/255 complete native images. The unchanged NativeUI provider/transport regression is reused from 7162a6ae, not counted as a new run.",
    "Candidate 01 fixes Gecko but misses Blink normal dispatch because the nonvirtual CheckboxInputType preactivation thunk contains a compiled duplicate body. Final adapter intercepts the owning HTMLInputElement journal entry instead, removing InputType layout decoding. Candidate 02 is build-only. Candidate 01 exact complete source provenance is not claimed; retain saved entry/header and binaries/raw observations.",
    "Early form tests sampled native tracking too soon or captured the actual cursor over the control. Final tests wait for native release/DOM click and move the cursor away. Firefox original checkbox y=34.5 exposed Python ties-to-even cropping at 34 while native paint snaps to 35; shared captures use floor(value+.5), with no pixel tolerance. A same-element recursive click expectation contradicted Blink original reentry suppression; final test verifies an independent nested untrusted checkbox click instead.",
    "The first dedicated Firefox control run reaches 26 passing rows then hits its existing 60-second harness deadline; no failed assertion or browser crash establishes a control regression. The isolated second run passes all 40 checks then its old postflight expects individual radio kind 3 but sees actual matrix kind 12. Its copied preset also enables native HTML buttons. Preserve both incomplete runs. The final dedicated preset uses its original individual radio and original HTML-button modes; the broad matrix mode remains covered separately."
  ],
  "open": [
    "Label pressed-state/animation, accessibility activation, complex author styles/control content and broader model mutation/lifetime cases.",
    "Radio topology/visibility/geometry, large-group efficiency, browser scaling/zoom/build variants and actual session-supervisor group recovery.",
    "Remaining browser controls, complete detached-menu/native-shortcut behavior, accessibility/IME, Chromium/Firefox derivatives and installed deployment. GTK/Qt/KDE follow browser work via the same layer.",
    "Browser toolbar/address bar/tabs keep existing components; future requested UI changes are optional per-app patches above the shared library and bridge."
  ],
